  "goodToKnow": "Der Schwimmer (die Schwimmerin) is a swimmer. German public pools have a Schwimmerbecken (deep pool for swimmers) and a Nichtschwimmerbecken (shallow pool). Children earn the Seepferdchen badge (little seahorse) as a first swimming certificate, then Bronze, Silber and Gold. The DLRG warns that more and more children can't swim well. In engineering, der Schwimmer is a float, as in a toilet cistern. Plural: die Schwimmer."
